  "query_preview": "..\n(Saturday night through Thursday)\nIssued at 1212 AM CDT Fri Sep 11 2026\n\nFor early next week, mid and upper level high pressure will \ninitially be centered over the southern Great Plains. The center \nof this high pressure will move eastward with time and eventually \nsettle over the Smoky Mountain region of Tennessee. This area of \nhigh pressure will continue to strengthen into the middle to late \nportion of the upcoming week, resulting in high pressure gradually\nbuilding in from the east. This is expected to keep our forecast \nmostly dry along with above normal temperatures. Some late \nafternoon convection may be possible over the coastal plains \nregion as the seabreeze moves inland. Any rain chances would \nlikely remain low.",
